MID: 69af1528a1375e44145856ac069652a4
STATEMENT: >>>
**Status: accepted design-time risk inventory; runtime acceptance not claimed.** The source model is [`threagile/model.yaml`](https://github.com/yohn-jp/codexia/blob/main/docs/architecture/threagile/model.yaml). Product behavior, authorization, persistence, deployment and recovery semantics remain owned by the referenced normative design documents and [LINK: DOC-REQUIREMENT-REGISTER, requirement register].

Threagile owns threat scenarios, assets, trust boundaries, risk identifiers and mitigations. The [LikeC4 model](https://github.com/yohn-jp/codexia/blob/main/docs/architecture/likec4/model.likec4) owns C4 structure and trust relationships. G5 checks LikeC4 element boundaries and required/forbidden relations, plus the required Threagile risk-to-boundary and risk-to-asset assignments. Those selected structural invariants correspond to the approved API, PostgreSQL, external MCP, Cloudflare, protected operations, backup and public Pages surfaces; neither model certifies deployment or attack resistance.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
MID: fc9beea335e84a7dfba950ec8aacc79c
UID: DOC-ARCHITECTURE-THREAT-MODEL-tracked-risks
TITLE: Tracked risks

[TEXT]
MID: 377ee57239826b1c825103282e81d5db
STATEMENT: >>>
| Threagile risk ID | Design references | Existing verification references | Threat focus | Tracking state |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `codexia-bola-project-isolation` | REQ-AUTH-002, REQ-DATA-003 | AUTH-06, MCPV-004; [LINK: DOC-VERIFICATION-TRACEABILITY-REGISTER, traceability register] | Object or project identifier crosses an authorization boundary | `unchecked` |
| `codexia-mcp-issuer-resource` | REQ-AUTH-001, REQ-AUTH-003, REQ-MCP-001 | EXT-MCP-001, AUTH-05/06, MCPV-002/004 | OAuth issuer, resource, client assignment or MCP scope is confused | `unchecked` |
| `codexia-session-scope-confusion` | REQ-AUTH-002, REQ-AUTH-003, REQ-AUTH-005 | EXT-AUTH-001, EXT-SHARE-001, AUTH-04/05/06; REQ-AUTH-005 remains unmapped | Owner, browser session, external MCP client and reader disclosure scopes are confused | `unchecked` |
| `codexia-false-db-receipt` | REQ-DATA-002, REQ-API-002 | REQ-DATA-002:O01, REQ-API-002:O01, MCPV-005; [LINK: DOC-VERIFICATION-TRACEABILITY-REGISTER, existing E2E candidate] | A mutation is reported as committed without a durable PostgreSQL revision receipt | `unchecked` |
| `codexia-edge-operations-plane` | REQ-EXT-001, REQ-OPS-001, REQ-OPS-002 | EXT-EDGE-001/002, EXT-OPS-001, AUTH-07, G5 | Public Cloudflare routing is mistaken for project authorization or host administration | `unchecked` |
| `codexia-backup-key-restore` | REQ-OPS-003, REQ-OPS-004, REQ-OPS-005 | EXT-OPS-003, BACKUP-S3-001–007, BKC-T04–08 and BKC-T10 | Age key separation, ciphertext identity, independent receipt or isolated restore fails | `unchecked` |
| `codexia-public-pages-disclosure` | REQ-EXT-002, REQ-QUAL-002 | AUTH-08, G5; `scripts/audit/portal.test.mjs` | A public static architecture artifact contains credentials or private source data | `unchecked` |

These are references to the repository's requirement, interface, and acceptance identifiers, not claims that the referenced runtime tests passed. Their current mapped/unverified, unmapped, or unimplemented status remains authoritative in the [LINK: DOC-VERIFICATION-TRACEABILITY-REGISTER, traceability register]. The `check` field for every risk carries the exact references and is validated by G5.

The `risk_tracking` entries use wildcard patterns to bind each category to its generated Threagile risk instances. Every risk remains `unchecked`; the listed mitigations are design controls that require separate implementation and runtime evidence. No risk is marked `mitigated` or `false-positive` by this model.
<<<

